  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "SeaTac DGC is the biggest round in the Seattle metro — 27 holes, nearly 10,000 feet, par 87, laid out through a former neighborhood under the constant flight paths of SeaTac Airport. Keith Lionetti's design mixes open fields with wooded tunnels, flat ground with serious length.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Mach X baskets, it's the course where Seattle players go when they want to throw a lot of disc golf in one visit. The airport traffic overhead is part of the charm — you'll never mistake this course for anywhere else.",
    "Bring your longest discs and your stamina. The first 18 are already a full round; the last nine are a bonus that most players choose to take."
  ],
