  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 21 is the longest at SeaTac at 547 feet — a par 4 that captures the course's whole character: open ground, real distance, and the planes roaring overhead. A big drive down the fairway, then a long approach to a basket that sits in the open with nowhere to hide. It's the hole that makes 27 holes feel like exactly the right number.",
  "localTips": "Bring water and your longest discs — this is a 10,000-foot round. The first 18 are the full course; the bonus nine is worth playing if you have the legs. Free to play, flat and cart friendly, and the airport noise is part of the experience.",
